      "before": "Among the state’s four electric distribution companies, Rockland Electric Company will see the largest monthly decrease, though overall bills will remain roughly unchanged at each of the utilities.",
      "highlight": "The average Rockland customer using about 650 kilowatt-hours within a billing cycle can expect their bill to decrease by 67 cents, board staff said, and ratepayers with Atlantic City Electric will pay 5 cents less each month.",
      "after": "The average Jersey Central Power and Light customer will see their bill drop by 8 cents. Average monthly electric bills with PSE&G were expected to rise by 2 cents as a result of transmission rates flowing from the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission, but board staff said state offsets would eliminate the increase. Gas rates will decline further."
    },
